Today I did more reading and learned:
1. Solar panels use photovoltaic (PV) cells, which contain semiconductor materials that absorb sunlight and convert it into electrical energy.
2. Solar panel efficiency measures how much of the sunlight received is successfully converted into electricity. Not all sunlight becomes usable energy.
3. The amount of electricity a solar panel produces depends on factors such as sunlight intensity, panel efficiency, panel size, temperature, and shading.
4. Solar panels are made by connecting multiple smaller photovoltaic cells together to increase their total power output.
5. The position and angle of a solar panel affect how much sunlight it receives. A panel that tracks the Sun can generally collect more daily sunlight than one that stays fixed.

